# Copy this file to .env.local (that filename is git-ignored) and fill in
# the real values from your Supabase project: Project Settings → API.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is called "anon" / "public" in that screen — it is
# SAFE to put in frontend code, it's designed to be public. Row Level
# Security (see supabase/schema.sql) is what actually protects the data.
#
# Never put the "service_role" key here or anywhere in this app — that key
# bypasses Row Level Security entirely and must never reach the browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional — error monitoring (Sentry). Leave blank to run without it;
# nothing else in this app depends on it working. A DSN isn't secret —
# it's meant to be embedded in the browser bundle, same as the anon key
# above — get one at sentry.io → Create Project → platform React →
# Settings → Client Keys (DSN). See "Error monitoring (Sentry)" in the
# README before changing the connect-src in netlify.toml if you swap in
# your own project — that CSP directive has to name your DSN's ingest
# host or the browser silently blocks the SDK's own error reports.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
